        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: How She Move\n- People: Ian Iqbal Rashid, Rutina Wesley, Clé Bennett, Romina D'Ugo, Annmarie Morais\n- Concepts: step dancing, stepping\n- Topics: street culture, African-American performance\n\nFacts:\n- Annmarie Morais was born in 1973 in Jamaica.\n- Annmarie Morais is a Jamaican-Canadian screenwriter best known for writing the film How She Move.\n- How She Move is a 2007 drama film directed by Ian Iqbal Rashid and starring Rutina Wesley, Clé Bennett, and Romina D'Ugo.\n- How She Move showcases the street culture of step dancing.\n- Stepping may be performed by an individual, but it is generally performed by groups of three or more in arrangements that often resemble military formations.",
